cl. 1. P. गा॑यति, rarely Ā. ˚ते (1. sg. गा॑ये [RV. viii, 46, 17] & गायिषे [RV. vii, 96, 1] Lāṭy.; MBh. &c.), exceptionally cl. 2. गाति (MBh. iii, 15850; xii, 10299 : cl. 3. P. जिगाति, Dhātup. xxii, 20; perf. जगौ, AitBr. &c.; aor. अगासीत्; Prec. गेयात्, Pāṇ. vi, 4, 67; pr. p. P. गा॑यत्, RV. &c.; ind.p. गीत्वा [with prep. -गाय (Pāṇ. vi, 4, 69), AitBr., or -गी॑य, ŚBr. &c.]; inf. गातुम्),
to sing, speak or recite in a singing manner, sing to (dat. RV.), praise in song (with acc.), relate in metrical language, RV.; AV. &c.;
to sing before (acc.), Kathās. i, 53 :
Pass. गीय॑ते (p. ˚य॑मान), to be sung or praised in song, RV. &c.;
to be called, MBh. i, 4329; Kum. ii, 5; Kathās. xci (perf. जगे), &c.:
Caus. गापयति (

. pl. गाययेयुर्, JaimUp.), to cause to sing or praise in song, Lāṭy.; ŚāṅkhGṛ.; Ragh.; BhP. &c.:
Intens. जेगीयते (Pāṇ. vi, 4, 66), to sing, MBh. xii, 12200;
to be sung or praised in song, VarBṛS. xix, 18; Daś. i, 6;
to be asserted obstinately, Sarvad. iii, 224; xii, 1;
